Peak current (amperage) and pulse-on time (pulse duration) are the process parameters that most affect material removal rate (MRR). {{cite:S1#c1}}  
Multiple studies identify peak current as the dominant factor for MRR (86.43% effect in one ANOVA) and show pulse-on time as the next-most important parameter in Taguchi designs. {{cite:S2#c1}}{{cite:S1#c1}}  
Separate ANOVA work on EDM also reports amperage as overwhelmingly influential for MRR (99.66% in that study). {{cite:S8#c1}}  
In short, studies consistently agree that increasing peak current (amperage) and longer pulse-on time raise MRR; the exact relative importance varies by study and experimental design. {{cite:S2#c1}}{{cite:S1#c1}}

